{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>One language.</b> The holy tongue." "<b>And few words.</b> They came to one counsel and said: It is not enough for Him that He has chosen for Himself the upper ones — let us go up to the firmament and make war against Him. Another interpretation: against the Unique One of the world. Another interpretation of ״וּדְבָרִים אֲחָדִים״ — they said: Once every one thousand two hundred and ninety-six years the firmament collapses, just as it did in the days of the Flood — come, let us make supports for it (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The phrase שֶׁיָּבֹר לוֹ אֶת הָעֶלְיוֹנִים is rendered hyper-literally; the idiom בחר is taken as 'choose,' with the object העליונים = 'the upper ones,' i.e., the heavens."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:17.294759059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}